Exception Handling
-------------------

An exception is:

An unwanted event that occurs during program execution and disrupts normal flow.

Program crashes immediately without Exception Handling.

Why Exception Handling?
--------------------------
To:
    prevent abrupt termination
    continue program execution
    handle errors gracefully


    try {
        // risky code
    }
    catch(ExceptionType e) {
        // handling code
    }
    finally {
        // always executes
                    Used mainly for:
                        closing files
                        database connections
                        cleanup code
                        releasing resources
    }


Working Internally
-------------------
When exception occurs:
    JVM creates exception object
    JVM stops normal flow
    Searches matching catch block
    Executes catch block
    Continues remaining program
 try → exception occurs → matching catch → continue program


Common Exception Types
-------------------
    NullPointerException
    ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException
    ArithmeticException
    NumberFormatException
    FileNotFoundException
    IOException
    ClassNotFoundException
    IllegalArgumentException
    IllegalStateException
    RuntimeException
    Exception (base class for all exceptions)